<title>BELGIUM: EU to clear Lyonnaise/Suez merger. [CORRECTED 12:00 GMT]</title>
<headline>EU to clear Lyonnaise/Suez merger. [CORRECTED 12:00 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>European commissioner Karel Van Miert said on Tuesday that the Commission would in the next few days clear the merger between Lyonnaise Des Eaux and Compagnie de Suez after Lyonnaise unit Sita agreed to divest some waste treatment assets in Belgium.</p>
<p>(Corrects from &quot;..Suez's unit Tractebel agreed to divest its waste management business in Belgium.&quot;)</p>
<p>&quot;Both companies are active in this market. Once the problem was indentified they had a choice between offering fully fledged remedies or we would have gone into a second phase (detailed probe),&quot; Van Miert said as he arrived for a conference.</p>
<p>He added that the two partners had agreed at the end of last week to address the Commission's concerns.</p>
<p>-- Brussels newsroom 32 2 287 6830</p>
